<Layout
  title="About | Vignesh Guruswami">
  <h1>About Me</h1>
  <p>
  Hey there, my name is Vignesh Guruswami. I'm not too great at summing up my 
  personality and accomplishments in a brief and succinct way, but i'll give 
  a crack at it. I'm a 24 year old software/firmware engineer that loves all 
  things outdoors and physics related. I have a passion for building silly 
  projects and breaking my body through rock climbing. Sometimes I get those 
  verbs confused and end up breaking my personal projects instead, 
  but they don't seem to mind too much.
  </p>

  <p>
  While I can't call my expertise multidisciplinary, I have plenty of 
  experience working on large scale projects alongside electrical and 
  mechanical engineers, and have picked up a lot of skills along the way. 
  One example is my work with radio systems and a controls for a cube 
  satellite in SJSU's <a href="https://cube3sjsu.org">CubeSat program</a>. 
  You tend to learn a couple things working alongside mechanical engineers, 
  which is how I learned about Control Theory and its applications.
  </p>

  <p>
  At the moment I'm currently searching for work. If any of my experience or 
  musings interest you, feel free to reach out to me through your platform of
  choice.
  </p>
</Layout>
